          "text": "Mood and sleep history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports mood as “up and down for ages,” with timing vague. Sleep is erratic: sometimes up all night on the phone and sometimes sleeping all day. Reports low motivation some days, staying in her room and feeling unable to be bothered."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Anger and behaviour"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports getting angry quickly; currently mainly yelling and slamming doors. No current physical aggression reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal thoughts and safety"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports passive thoughts of “what’s the point,” but denies plan or intent and says she would not act because her Nan would be upset. Future-oriented, discussing having her own place and doing a course. No current self-harm or suicidality reported; no past attempts disclosed. Assessment reliability limited by cognition and poor history."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Psychosis-related symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No clear psychotic symptoms elicited. Denies visual and auditory hallucinations when asked, and denies current auditory hallucinations. No clear delusions noted; history-taking was tangential."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
